{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"reasoning","text":"**Evaluating comment quality**\n\nI want to score comments neutrally, giving positive scores if they're well grounded. It’s important that the comments feel natural and flow logically. I should avoid using moderation templates or any internal IDs and slugs. If a title is mentioned, I can use a human title for reference. The main focus should be on how the body of the comment performs, without bringing in any commentary on the quality itself."}}
